# Power Profile Feature — Implementation Rules

Full plan: `docs/power-profile-framework-plan.md`. Read it before starting any phase.

---

## Folder Structure

All new code lives under `src/features/power-profile/`. Route files in `src/app/(app)/` are thin wrappers only.

```
src/features/power-profile/
├── constants.ts          # MIN_CALIBRATION_SAMPLES threshold (= 5)
├── types/                # All PPL/CI/session/athlete types
├── services/             # All calculation, persistence, detection logic
├── store/                # athlete-profile-store, power-session-store
├── hooks/                # Feature hooks only
├── components/           # Feature UI components
└── screens/              # Full-page screens
```

---

## Power Measurement Mode — Critical

**Never read power values directly in PPL services.** Always go through `power-source-service.resolveSprintPower()`.

The app uses a four-tier `PowerMeasurementMode`:

| Mode | When active |
|---|---|
| `'raw'` | Friction detection unavailable, calibration threshold not met |
| `'calibrated'` | ≥ 5 calibration sprints for this surface; derived × learned ratio |
| `'friction_corrected'` | Live friction detection at Medium/High confidence |
| `'fused'` | Both channels active and agree within 5% |

```ts
// ✅ Correct
const { power, mode } = resolveSprintPower(metrics, surfaceType, calibrationStats);

// ❌ Wrong — bypasses abstraction and loses mode metadata
const power = metrics.peakPower;
```

- Every sprint must stamp `powerMeasurementMode` with the resolved mode
- `calibration-service.updateCalibration(athleteProfile, sprint)` is called after each sprint save **only when both `frictionCorrectedPower` and `derivedPower` are available**
- `frictionConfidence` defaults to `'Unknown'` — never block on it
- `'calibrated'` activates automatically once `MIN_CALIBRATION_SAMPLES` (5) are met for a surface — no user action needed

